## Usage

```go
import (
	orm "{{ .ModulePath }}"
	types "{{ .TypesModule }}"
)

db, err := orm.Connect(ctx, connString)
if err != nil {
	return err
}
defer db.Close()
{{ with index .Repositories 0 }}
record, err := db.{{ .TypeName }}.GetOne(ctx, id, nil)
{{- end }}
```

Repositories expose `GetOne`, `GetManyByIDs`, `FindOne`, `FindMany`,
`FindPage`, `CreateOne`, `CreateMany`, `UpdateOne`, `UpdateMany`, `DeleteOne`,
and `DeleteMany`. Versioned tables also expose `GetVersion`, `ListVersions`,
`GetAsOf`, `UpdateOneIfVersion`, and `DeleteOneIfVersion`, which soft-deletes
a table with soft deletes and hard-deletes one without. Tables with soft
deletes additionally expose `HardDeleteOne`.
{{- if .HasOptimisticTables }}
Optimistic tables expose `UpdateOneIfVersion` and `DeleteOneIfVersion` too,
but keep no history, so they have no `GetVersion`, `ListVersions`, or
`GetAsOf`.
{{- end }}

Each `*Update` type has `ApplyTo(*types.T)` to project set and `SetNull`
fields onto a stored row, and `New*SnapshotUpdate` to build a full
replacement from a complete value.

`<Type>FilterConditions(filter, &args)` gives a filter's conditions, each
column qualified by its table, for a query of your own: its values are
appended to `args`, their placeholders numbered after those already there.
{{- if .HasSearch }}
A table with search fields (`@searchField`) has `SearchText` on its filter,
which keeps the rows whose `search_text` holds each of its words, in any
case.
{{- end }}

`FindPage(ctx, filter, opts)` reads a page of the rows a filter finds, in a
`<Type>Sort`'s order of one column, ties broken by the primary key: one query
of `Limit + 1` rows after `After`, and no count. The page's `Next` is the
`<Type>PageKey` of its last row when more rows follow, which the next page
takes as `After`. `Parse<Type>Sort` reads a page request's sort, `name` or
`-name`, and refuses a field the table cannot sort by; an `After` of another
sort is `ErrPageKey`.
{{- if .VersionGraphs }}

## Version graphs

A version graph's facade (`db.<Name>Graph()`) creates refs, saves edits on
them, commits, seals, merges, reverts, and reads a commit's or a ref's tree.
It turns typed edits into canonical rows and runs each operation on the
version-graph engine, `{{ .Naming.VersionGraphGoModule }}/engine`, over its
Postgres adapter in a transaction of the ORM's pool. The engine drives the
version-graph core through its Go binding, which links the core's static
archive through cgo. Build the archive from a superschematic checkout with
`scripts/versiongraph-archive.sh` and put the directory it prints in
`CGO_LDFLAGS` as `-L<dir>`; a `replace` directive to that checkout finds it
without the flag.
{{- end }}
